          "title": "Define one, then call it",
          "weight": 1,
          "config": {
            "title": "Define one, then call it",
            "instructions": "The body of the function is indented under the def. The call is not — it is back at the left, and it is the line that actually makes anything happen.",
            "language": "python",
            "indentSize": 4,
            "maxIndent": 1,
            "lines": [
              { "id": "a", "text": "def greet():" },
              { "id": "b", "text": "print(\"Hello!\")" },
              { "id": "c", "text": "print(\"Welcome to Nybble\")" },
              { "id": "d", "text": "greet()" }
            ]
          },
          "key": {
            "solution": [
              { "id": "a", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "b", "indent": 1 },
              { "id": "c", "indent": 1 },
              { "id": "d", "indent": 0 }
            ],
            "distractors": [],
            "marks": 4,
            "partial": true,
            "distractorPenalty": 0,
            "explanation": "Defining a function does not run it — it only gives the block a name. Nothing at all is printed until the last line calls it. The brackets are what make it a call: greet on its own would just name the function.",
            "check": { "stdout": "Hello!\nWelcome to Nybble\n" }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "runner_id": "parsons",
          "title": "An argument in, a value out",
          "weight": 1,
          "config": {
            "title": "An argument in, a value out",
            "instructions": "This one takes a number and hands an answer back, so the call goes on the right of an = sign.",
            "language": "python",
            "indentSize": 4,
            "maxIndent": 1,
            "lines": [
              { "id": "a", "text": "def double(number):" },
              { "id": "b", "text": "return number * 2" },
              { "id": "c", "text": "answer = double(7)" },
              { "id": "d", "text": "print(\"Twice 7 is\", answer)" }
            ]
          },
          "key": {
            "solution": [
              { "id": "a", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "b", "indent": 1 },
              { "id": "c", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "d", "indent": 0 }
            ],
            "distractors": [],
            "marks": 4,
            "partial": true,
            "distractorPenalty": 0,
            "explanation": "number is a name that only exists inside the function; the 7 in the call is what it stands for on this run. return ends the function and hands the value back to whoever called it, which is how answer gets its value.",
            "check": { "stdout": "Twice 7 is 14\n" }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "runner_id": "parsons",
          "title": "Return, not print",
          "weight": 1,
          "config": {
            "title": "Return, not print",
            "instructions": "The function is called twice and the two answers are then added together. One of the wrong lines shows the answer instead of handing it back — which looks the same on screen until the last line runs.",
            "language": "python",
            "indentSize": 4,
            "maxIndent": 2,
            "lines": [
              { "id": "a", "text": "def area(width, height):" },
              { "id": "b", "text": "return width * height" },
              { "id": "c", "text": "first = area(3, 4)" },
              { "id": "d", "text": "second = area(5, 6)" },
              { "id": "e", "text": "print(\"First area:\", first)" },
              { "id": "f", "text": "print(\"Second area:\", second)" },
              { "id": "g", "text": "print(\"Total:\", first + second)" },
              { "id": "d1", "text": "print(width * height)" },
              { "id": "d2", "text": "def area(width, height)" },
              { "id": "d3", "text": "return width + height" }
            ]
          },
          "key": {
            "solution": [
              { "id": "a", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "b", "indent": 1 },
              { "id": "c", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "d", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "e", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "f", "indent": 0 },
              { "id": "g", "indent": 0 }
            ],
            "distractors": ["d1", "d2", "d3"],
            "marks": 7,
            "partial": true,
            "distractorPenalty": 1,
            "explanation": "A function that prints its answer cannot be used in a sum. Swap the return for a print and the two areas appear on screen, but first and second both end up as None and the last line stops with a TypeError. The def line needs its colon, and an area is a multiplication.",
            "check": { "stdout": "First area: 12\nSecond area: 30\nTotal: 42\n" }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "p4",
          "runner_id": "parsons",
          "title": "A default argument",
          "weight": 1,
          "config": {
