            "distractors": ["d1", "d2", "d3"],
            "marks": 4,
            "partial": true,
            "distractorPenalty": 1,
            "explanation": "An argument with a default has to come after the ones without, or Python refuses the definition — it would have no way to tell which value you meant. Without the default, the first call would fail for want of a second argument, and greet() with nothing at all fails either way because name has no default.",
            "check": { "stdout": "Hello, Aoife\nGood morning, Ben\n" }
          }
        },
        {
