            "distractorPenalty": 1,
            "explanation": "The return is at indent 1, after the loop has finished — inside the loop it would end the function on the very first number. A list can be passed to a function like any other value. Returning only one of the two leaves the other unavailable to the caller, and taking the pair into a single variable gives you both stuck together rather than two usable numbers.",
            "check": { "stdout": "Total: 210\nAverage: 70.0\n" }
